#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:0
msgid ""
"Complete reference for snap's system architecture, including snapd, the Snap "
"Store, Linux security modules, interfaces, and services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:8
msgid "System architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:10
msgid ""
"The snap packaging system consists of many components, from system-level "
"Linux kernel security modules, managed by the snap daemon, _snapd_, to the "
"network connected Snap Store for package retrieval and updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:12
msgid ""
"These components inter-communicate and operate together to create a secure "
"and confined execution environment for application and service deployment. "
"The overall process with these components and their communication is "
"outlined below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:14
msgid "System process overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:16
msgid ""
"![Snap system process overview, showing how the snap daemon, snapd, manages "
"snaps within a sandbox and configures the system security modules for access|"
"666x500](/images/system-architecture.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:16
msgid ""
"Snap system process overview, showing how the snap daemon, snapd, manages "
"snaps within a sandbox and configures the system security modules for access|"
"666x500"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:18
msgid ""
"**Figure: Snap system process overview, showing how the snap daemon, snapd, "
"manages snaps within a sandbox and configures the system security modules "
"for access.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:20
msgid ""
"The snap daemon, **snapd**,  handles **snap management** to configure and "
"maintain each snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:22
msgid ""
"The snap daemon also maintains the **security configuration** that creates "
"the **sandbox** for both snap executables and data. This is implemented "
"using various **security modules** of the **Linux kernel**, including "
"Seccomp, AppArmor and Cgroups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:24
msgid ""
"Snaps have the least possible privileges by default. Additional system "
"resources are permitted through the **{ref}`interfaces <explanation-"
"interfaces-all-about-interfaces>`** mechanism which changes the security "
"profile for each snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:26
msgid ""
"A **snap package** is a self-contained and immutable _SquashFS_ file "
"carrying application-specific content alongside metadata to tell the system "
"how it should be manipulated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:28
msgid ""
"Package **downloads and updates** are managed through a connection to the "
"remote **Snap Store**, which includes package integrity and validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:30
msgid "Security modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:32
msgid ""
"The snap daemon uses privilege isolation mechanisms rooted in the Linux "
"kernel through Cgroups and Namespaces, AppArmor and Seccomp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:0
msgid ""
"**Cgroups** Limit the amount of resources and which devices the process "
"confined to a snap can consume (CPU, memory, network bandwidth, and so on)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:0
msgid ""
"**Namespaces** Make sure processes in a snap see their own personal view of "
"the system (files, processes, network interfaces, hostname, and so on)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:0
msgid ""
"**AppArmor** Allows system administrators to restrict snap capabilities with "
"default security profiles that can be extended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:0
msgid ""
"**Seccomp** Isolates processes running in a snap by limiting the system "
"calls they are allowed to make."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:39
msgid ""
"The state of snapd, and many of its key functions, can be accessed through "
"its {ref}`REST API <reference-development-snapd-rest-api>`, enabling remote "
"device configuration, updates and orchestration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:41
msgid "System process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:43
msgid ""
"**snapd -> Snap Store** : retrieves snap and assertion data from the package "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:44
msgid ""
"**snapd -> AppArmor**: sets up security profiles using permissions and "
"capabilities by creating AppArmor profiles for each and modifying them "
"whenever new interfaces are connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:45
msgid ""
"**snapd -> Seccomp**: as with AppArmor, uses per-snap profiles to limit the "
"system calls a snap can make."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:47
msgid "For services:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:48
msgid ""
"**snapd -> systemd** : handles mounting, sockets, Cgroup limits and tracks "
"service lifecycles for each snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:50
msgid "Process components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:52
msgid ""
"The package ecosystem can be separated at the binary level, including the "
"socket files, and these components include the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:54
msgid ""
"**snap packages**:  each snap is a _SquashFS_ file carrying content "
"alongside metadata to tell the system how it should be manipulated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:55
msgid ""
"**snapd**: the background service that manages, maintains, installs and "
"removes snap packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:56
msgid ""
"**snap**: the command-line interface for interacting with snap functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:57
msgid ""
"**snap-confine**: used internally to set up the confinement and namespaces "
"for individual snaps before executing into the snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:58
msgid ""
"**snapctl**: used from within the running snap environment to access snap "
"management functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:59
msgid "`/run/snapd.socket`: Unix socket used by snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:60
msgid "`/run/snapd-snap.socket`: Unix socket used by snapctl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:62
msgid "Process component relationships"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:64
msgid "**snapd -> `/run/snapd.socket`**:  exposes REST API through"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:65
msgid "**snapd -> `/run/snapd-snap.socket`**: exposes REST API through"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:66
msgid "**snap -> `/run/snapd.socket`**: makes user requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:67
msgid "**snapctl -> `/run/snapd-snap.socket`**: makes snap requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:68
msgid ""
"**snaps -> `snapctl`**: uses snap management features exposed by *snapd*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/system-architecture.md:69
msgid "**snapd -> `snap run`**: prepares confinement/execs into snap"
msgstr ""
